A||||7||FieroMike||1985 GT 4speed or 5-speed?
Z||000000||FieroMike||04-25-99||12:36 PM||||I have been wondering this since I bought my car and was wondering if anybody can find the answer!  From all the information that I have, '85 GT's only came with 4 speeds.  Yet my car has a 5-speed.  Also the two cables coming off the transmission go directly through my air intake hose, I have to bend them way down and tie them off so that it doesn't hit anything, was this tranny put on by someone?  Or is Pontiac's design way off? Any answers would be greatly appreciated! Thanx
Z||000001||Rob||04-25-99||03:37 PM||||I also have an 85 GT, at all the shows and people I have talked with I have not heard of  a five speed factory installed. Someone most likely put it in.    
Z||000002||FieroMike||04-25-99||03:58 PM||||Thanks, that's was I was thinking.  Do you think that the air intake is plumbed differently on the 5 speeds, mine goes straight from the TB across and down, I have seen a 5-speed were it comes back towards the back of the car first then goes into the can at an angle.  Thanx again.
Z||000003||Michael Radak||04-25-99||08:38 PM||||Hi, no they didn't make any 5 speed for an '85 GT Fiero.  That was an option in '86.  Those 5 speeds were only on the 4's (iron duke).
Z||000004||PaUL||04-26-99||02:19 PM||||FieroMike:<br>you say the cables are on top? if so sounds like a 5spd isuzu trans, the getrage 5spds have the cable on the bottom.
Z||000005||FieroMike||04-26-99||02:27 PM||||PaUL,<br>Really??  What kind of ISUZU?  Which transmission is better, getrag or Izuzu?  It seems to work really nicely, I have no problems shifting like everyone else!! Thanks for the info.
Z||000006||PaUL||04-26-99||03:21 PM||||the Isuzu transmission Im refering to is the 5spds that came with the 84-87 4 cycl fieros. All earlier V6 Fieros came with a 4spd muncie. The 5 spd Isuzu was not offered with the v6 because it wasnt supposed to be strong enough to handle the power of the v6. Ways to cope with this are described in another post. Im using an Isuzu trans with a 2.8v6.<p>BTW a long time ago, in the 80s I remember reading a Readers Digest article about how GMs Muncie transmission div. beat Isuzu in an intra corp. competition to design and produce a 5 spd for the 2.8 V6. GM has a controlling interest in Isuzu owning more than %50 of the stock making it more a GM div. than a rival company. <br>
Z||000007||FieroMike||04-26-99||03:27 PM||||Thanks a lot PaUL. That is some good information.  I had the image of someone talking the tranny out of a Rodeo or something!!! Thanks again!
